  <meiHead>
    <fileDesc>
      <titleStmt>
        <title>Diffusa est</title>
      </titleStmt>
      <pubStmt/>
      <notesStmt>
        <annot>Pitches: Corpus Monodicum (Akademie der Wissenschaften und der Literatur Mainz / Universität Würzburg), document Gr 807-0194-4GS, https://stagedata.corpus-monodicum.de/mei/77f4b16b-85b8-457e-aa92-0ef1958cfccf/Gr%20807-0194-4GS.xml, which transcribes the Graduale Synopticum (Universität Regensburg; database by Xaver Kainzbauer), no. 0194; © Corpus Monodicum; read an octave lower. Neume division and names of Diffusa est gratia in and tu- after Stefan Morent's MEI (15 May 2026), where his notes agree in number and contour; elsewhere one group per syllable as in the Graduale Synopticum. The turn from f. 23r to 23v before "bi" is taken from the facsimile.</annot>
      </notesStmt>
      <sourceDesc>
        <source>
          <bibl>
            <title>Diffusa est</title>
            <idno type="siglum">A-Gu</idno>
            <idno type="shelfmark">Ms. 807</idno>
            <ptr target="https://unipub.uni-graz.at/obvugrscript/content/pageview/5564630"/>
            <idno type="cantus-id">g01397</idno>
            <note type="genre">Gradual</note>
            <note type="mode">5</note>
            <note label="manuscript" type="description">Gradual, 12th century, olim Klosterneuburg/Passau (after the source list of the Graduale Synopticum); on ff. 23r–23v neumes on a staff with letter clefs.</note>
            <note label="manuscript" type="transcription">Merged from two transcriptions (graz-807-merged.mei, merge_graz_807.py): pitches from Corpus Monodicum (Akademie der Wissenschaften und der Literatur Mainz / Universität Würzburg), document Gr 807-0194-4GS, https://stagedata.corpus-monodicum.de/mei/77f4b16b-85b8-457e-aa92-0ef1958cfccf/Gr%20807-0194-4GS.xml, which transcribes the Graduale Synopticum (Universität Regensburg; database by Xaver Kainzbauer), no. 0194; © Corpus Monodicum; read an octave lower. Neume division and names of Diffusa est gratia in and tu- after Stefan Morent's MEI (15 May 2026), where his notes agree in number and contour.</note>
          </bibl>
        </source>
      </sourceDesc>
    </fileDesc>
